{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NCvvU59RPwoyo7JhdkTo27","type":"tool_result","content":"214\t### 4. Memory Graph\n215\t\n216\tMemory should be stored as typed claims and episodes, not loose notes.\n217\t\n218\tPrimary memory classes:\n219\t\n220\t- `Observation`\n221\t- `Decision`\n222\t- `Constraint`\n223\t- `Pattern`\n224\t- `AntiPattern`\n225\t- `WorkflowOutcome`\n226\t- `FailurePattern`\n227\t- `Procedure`\n228\t- `Preference`\n229\t- `ArchitectureInvariant`\n230\t- `DocsContract`\n231\t- `OpenQuestion`\n232\t- `CounterMemory` — a memory record that explicitly asserts a prior memory is wrong or no longer applicable. Distinct from a `contradicts` link: a link connects two existing memories; a CounterMemory is a first-class record authored by an agent or user that carries its own evidence, scope, and verification status and can itself be superseded or invalidated. Use CounterMemory when the counter-claim needs its own provenance and lifecycle, not just an edge annotation.\n233\t\n234\tEach memory record requires:\n235\t\n236\t- stable id\n237\t- content\n238\t- memory class\n239\t- assertion type\n240\t- scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization\n241\t- verification status\n242\t- confidence and confidence reason\n243\t- freshness policy\n244\t- validity conditions\n245\t- invalidation triggers\n246\t- provenance events\n247\t- evidence references\n248\t- linked files\n249\t- linked symbols\n250\t- linked docs\n251\t- linked tests\n252\t- linked memories\n253\t- contradiction links\n254\t- supersession links\n255\t- access history\n256\t- usefulness scores\n257\t- last verified state\n258\t\n259\tMemory links should be first-class records:\n260\t\n261\t- source memory\n262\t- target memory or graph node\n263\t- link type\n264\t- strength\n265\t- reason\n266\t- evidence event\n267\t- created by\n268\t- created at\n269\t- verification status\n270\t\n271\tRequired link types:\n272\t\n273\t- `supports`\n274\t- `contradicts`\n275\t- `supersedes`\n276\t- `refines`\n277\t- `generalizes`\n278\t- `specializes`\n279\t- `co_occurs_with`\n280\t- `derived_from`\n281\t- `applies_to`\n282\t- `validated_by`\n283\t- `invalidated_by`\n284\t\n285\t### 5. Working Memory\n286\t\n287\tWorking memory is per-task and short-lived. It should be explicit rather than implicit prompt accumulation.\n288\t\n289\tWorking memory contains:\n290\t\n291\t- task statement\n292\t- interpreted intent\n293\t- active files and symbols\n294\t- active hypotheses\n295\t- active failures\n296\t- current plan\n297\t- selected memories\n298\t- excluded memories and reasons\n299\t- budget decisions\n300\t- unresolved questions\n301\t- verification status\n302\t\n303\tRequired operations:\n304\t\n305\t- `retrieve`\n306\t- `summarize`\n307\t- `filter`\n308\t- `pin`\n309\t- `evict`\n310\t- `expand`\n311\t- `compress`\n312\t- `checkpoint`\n313\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"623701ab-dc49-4054-96ef-292da32369e2","uuid":"011b8dbd-9b76-464e-a959-28aed11cb125","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:10:09.563Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"### 4. Memory Graph\n\nMemory should be stored as typed claims and episodes, not loose notes.\n\nPrimary memory classes:\n\n- `Observation`\n- `Decision`\n- `Constraint`\n- `Pattern`\n- `AntiPattern`\n- `WorkflowOutcome`\n- `FailurePattern`\n- `Procedure`\n- `Preference`\n- `ArchitectureInvariant`\n- `DocsContract`\n- `OpenQuestion`\n- `CounterMemory` — a memory record that explicitly asserts a prior memory is wrong or no longer applicable. Distinct from a `contradicts` link: a link connects two existing memories; a CounterMemory is a first-class record authored by an agent or user that carries its own evidence, scope, and verification status and can itself be superseded or invalidated. Use CounterMemory when the counter-claim needs its own provenance and lifecycle, not just an edge annotation.\n\nEach memory record requires:\n\n- stable id\n- content\n- memory class\n- assertion type\n- scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization\n- verification status\n- confidence and confidence reason\n- freshness policy\n- validity conditions\n- invalidation triggers\n- provenance events\n- evidence references\n- linked files\n- linked symbols\n- linked docs\n- linked tests\n- linked memories\n- contradiction links\n- supersession links\n- access history\n- usefulness scores\n- last verified state\n\nMemory links should be first-class records:\n\n- source memory\n- target memory or graph node\n- link type\n- strength\n- reason\n- evidence event\n- created by\n- created at\n- verification status\n\nRequired link types:\n\n- `supports`\n- `contradicts`\n- `supersedes`\n- `refines`\n- `generalizes`\n- `specializes`\n- `co_occurs_with`\n- `derived_from`\n- `applies_to`\n- `validated_by`\n- `invalidated_by`\n\n### 5. Working Memory\n\nWorking memory is per-task and short-lived. It should be explicit rather than implicit prompt accumulation.\n\nWorking memory contains:\n\n- task statement\n- interpreted intent\n- active files and symbols\n- active hypotheses\n- active failures\n- current plan\n- selected memories\n- excluded memories and reasons\n- budget decisions\n- unresolved questions\n- verification status\n\nRequired operations:\n\n- `retrieve`\n- `summarize`\n- `filter`\n- `pin`\n- `evict`\n- `expand`\n- `compress`\n- `checkpoint`\n","numLines":100,"startLine":214,"totalLines":969}}}
